.\" Manpage for hostnamed
.TH HOSTNAMED 8 "October 2026" "hostnamed 0.3.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
hostnamed \- D-Bus hostname management daemon for non-systemd Linux systems
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B /usr/libexec/hostnamed
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hostnamed
is a standalone system daemon that implements the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1
D-Bus interface using direct D-Bus activation, with no dependency on
.IR systemd .
It exposes the same hostname and machine-identity properties as
.BR systemd-hostnamed (8)
on systemd-based distributions, allowing desktop tools such as
.B gnome-control-center
to read and edit the system's hostname and related machine metadata on
systems that use
.B elogind
and a D-Bus/PolKit stack without systemd.
.PP
.B hostnamed
does not poll or hold any files open for writing on its own initiative.
Instead it watches its source files with
.BR inotify (7)
and re-reads them whenever they change, regardless of who changed them
\(em the bundled
.BR hostnamectl (1)
client, a hand edit, or any other tool. After a resync it emits
.B PropertiesChanged
on the D-Bus object for every property whose value actually changed.
.PP
.B hostnamed
is normally started on demand by D-Bus activation when a client first
calls a method or reads a property on the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1
bus name. It can also be started manually for debugging.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Enable verbose debug logging to standard error in addition to syslog.
.SH "D-BUS INTERFACE"
.B hostnamed
registers the object
.B /org/freedesktop/hostname1
on the system bus, implementing the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1
interface.
.SS Properties
All properties are read-only over D-Bus; values are changed via the
.B Set*
methods described below, or by editing the underlying files directly
(see
.BR FILES ),
which
.B hostnamed
picks up through inotify. Property changes made by the daemon are
announced with
.B org.freedesktop.DBus.Properties.PropertiesChanged
when the effective value changes.
.TP
.B Hostname \fR(s)
The transient hostname, as returned by
.BR gethostname (2).
.TP
.B StaticHostname \fR(s)
The hostname persisted to the static hostname file (see
.BR FILES ).
.TP
.B PrettyHostname \fR(s)
A human-readable, free-form display name for the machine, stored as
.B PRETTY_HOSTNAME
in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
Unlike
.BR StaticHostname ,
this value is not used for name resolution and may contain spaces and
mixed case. When
.B SetPrettyHostname
receives a value that is itself a valid hostname, the daemon may reduce
it to the first label. Free-form values that merely contain dots, such as
.BR "Bob's PC v2.0" ,
are preserved as supplied.
.TP
.B DefaultHostname \fR(s)
The distribution default hostname, read from
.B DEFAULT_HOSTNAME
in
.IR /etc/os-release
when available, or
.B localhost
otherwise.
.TP
.B HostnameSource \fR(s)
One of
.RB ` static ',
.RB ` transient ',
or
.RB ` default ',
indicating which mechanism currently determines
.BR Hostname .
.TP
.B IconName \fR(s)
A freedesktop icon name (e.g.
.RB ` computer-desktop ',
.RB ` computer-laptop ')
describing the machine's form factor, taken from
.I /etc/machine-info
or derived from the SMBIOS chassis type when unset.
.TP
.B Chassis \fR(s)
A short chassis class string such as
.RB ` desktop ',
.RB ` laptop ',
.RB ` server ',
.RB ` tablet ',
or
.RB ` handset ',
taken from
.I /etc/machine-info
or derived from SMBIOS chassis-type data under
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id .
.TP
.B Deployment \fR(s)
A free-form deployment label (e.g.
.RB ` production ',
.RB ` staging '),
stored in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
.TP
.B Location \fR(s)
A free-form physical location string, stored in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
.TP
.B KernelName \fR(s)
The kernel name as reported by
.BR uname (2)
(typically
.RB ` Linux ').
.TP
.B KernelRelease \fR(s)
The kernel release string from
.BR uname (2).
.TP
.B KernelVersion \fR(s)
The kernel version string from
.BR uname (2).
.TP
.B OperatingSystemPrettyName \fR(s)
The
.B PRETTY_NAME
field from
.IR /etc/os-release .
.TP
.B OperatingSystemCPEName \fR(s)
The
.B CPE_NAME
field from
.IR /etc/os-release ,
if present.
.TP
.B OperatingSystemHomeURL \fR(s)
The
.B HOME_URL
field from
.IR /etc/os-release ,
if present.
.TP
.B HardwareVendor \fR(s)
The hardware vendor, selected from available DMI product and board vendor
fields, with a device-tree compatible-string fallback on platforms without
DMI.
.TP
.B HardwareModel \fR(s)
The hardware model, selected from available DMI product and board name fields,
with a device-tree model fallback on platforms without DMI.
.TP
.B FirmwareVersion \fR(s)
The BIOS/firmware version string, read from
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id/bios_version .
.TP
.B FirmwareDate \fR(t)
The BIOS/firmware release date, expressed as a
.B uint64
count of microseconds since the UNIX epoch (UTC), per the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1
interface specification. The value is parsed from the
.RB ` MM/DD/YYYY '
date string in
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id/bios_date .
If the source date is absent or cannot be parsed, this property is set
to
.BR UINT64_MAX .
.SS Methods
.TP
.B SetHostname(s name, b interactive)
Sets the transient hostname via
.BR sethostname (2).
Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-hostname
PolKit action.
.TP
.B SetStaticHostname(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
to the static hostname file (see
.BR FILES )
and updates the transient hostname to match. Passing an empty string
removes the static hostname file. Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-static-hostname
PolKit action.
.TP
.B SetPrettyHostname(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
as
.B PRETTY_HOSTNAME
in
.IR /etc/machine-info ,
after stripping any trailing dotted domain suffix (see
.B PrettyHostname
above). Requires the
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info
PolKit action.
.TP
.B SetIconName(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
as
.B ICON_NAME
in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
Requires
.BR org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info .
.TP
.B SetChassis(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
as
.B CHASSIS
in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
Requires
.BR org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info .
.TP
.B SetDeployment(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
as
.B DEPLOYMENT
in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
Requires
.BR org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info .
.TP
.B SetLocation(s name, b interactive)
Writes
.I name
as
.B LOCATION
in
.IR /etc/machine-info .
Requires
.BR org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info .
.TP
.B GetProductUUID(b interactive) \(-> ay
Returns the product UUID as 16 raw UUID bytes, read from
.IR /sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid .
Unreadable, malformed, or placeholder UUID values are reported as
.B org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.NotFound
rather than as an empty byte array.
.TP
.B GetHardwareSerial(b interactive) \(-> s
Returns the first usable serial number from the DMI product, board, or chassis
serial fields. Placeholder values are skipped. On systems without a usable
DMI serial, the device-tree serial-number property is used when available.
.TP
.B Describe() \(-> s
Returns a single JSON object containing the current value of every
property listed above, for clients that prefer one bulk read over
individual property gets. The bundled
.BR hostnamectl (1)
client uses this interface for changes; its status output currently reads
the underlying files directly.
.PP
For methods that take an
.I interactive
argument, a value of
.B true
indicates the caller is willing to wait for a PolKit authentication
dialog from the user's session PolKit agent. If authentication could
succeed only through interaction but
.B interactive
is
.BR false ,
the daemon returns
.B org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.InteractiveAuthorizationRequired .
Denied requests and operation failures are returned as D-Bus errors.
.SH AUTHORIZATION
Access to the
.B Set*
and
.B Get*
(UUID/serial) methods over D-Bus is controlled by
.BR polkit (8)
using the following actions, declared in
.IR /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.freedesktop.hostname1.policy :
.TP
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-hostname
.TQ
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-static-hostname
.TQ
.B org.freedesktop.hostname1.set-machine-info
.PP
The installed PolKit policy defines actions for hostname changes, machine-info
changes, and hardware identity reads. The rules file
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.freedesktop.hostname1.rules
allows root for hostname1 actions and grants the configured privileged
group (default
.RB ` wheel ',
see the
.B privileged-group
Meson option) access to the hostname-setting and machine-info actions.
Hardware UUID and serial reads have their own policy actions. Group
membership changes generally take effect after the user's next login
session.
.PP
These PolKit actions govern the bundled
.BR hostnamectl (1)
client's change requests as well as other D-Bus callers. The daemon performs the writes after authorization; the bundled client does
not write hostname configuration files directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/HOSTNAME
Default path for the static hostname file (Slackware convention; the
build-time
.B HOSTNAME
meson option, exposed in code as
.BR HOSTNAME_FILE ,
may point this elsewhere, e.g.
.I /etc/hostname
on other distributions). Watched with
.BR inotify (7).
.TP
.I /etc/machine-info
Stores
.BR PRETTY_HOSTNAME ", " ICON_NAME ", " CHASSIS ", " DEPLOYMENT ", "
and
.B LOCATION
as shell-style
.B KEY="value"
assignments. Updated atomically by the daemon while preserving unrelated
keys and comments. Watched with
.BR inotify (7).
.TP
.I /etc/os-release
Read for
.BR PRETTY_NAME ", " CPE_NAME ", "
and
.BR HOME_URL .
Not written by
.BR hostnamed .
.TP
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/chassis_type
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/chassis_serial
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/board_vendor
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/product_name
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/bios_version
.TQ
.I /sys/class/dmi/id/bios_date
SMBIOS/DMI sysfs nodes read for hardware and firmware identification.
Missing, unreadable, empty, or known placeholder values are skipped where
fallback fields are available. On device-tree systems, model, compatible,
chassis-type, and serial-number data may be used as fallbacks.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/actions/org.freedesktop.hostname1.policy
PolKit action declarations and default authorization requirements.
.TP
.I /usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/org.freedesktop.hostname1.rules
PolKit rules granting root access to hostname1 actions and the configured
privileged group access to hostname-setting and machine-info actions.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR hostnamectl (1),
.BR machine-info (5),
.BR os-release (5),
.BR polkit (8),
.BR pkcheck (1),
.BR sethostname (2),
.BR inotify (7)
